&lt;?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Blacksburg Museum and Cultural Foundation</title><link>http://localhost:1313/</link><description>Recent content on Blacksburg Museum and Cultural Foundation</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 05 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="http://localhost:1313/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>About</title><link>http://localhost:1313/about/</link><pubDate>Fri, 05 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>http://localhost:1313/about/</guid><description>&lt;p>The Blacksburg Museum and Cultural Foundation preserves the region’s stories through museum operations, exhibitions, education, and community engagement. We care for the Alexander Black House and St. Luke &amp;amp; Odd Fellows Hall, sharing local history and cultural heritage with visitors and learners.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Event Rental</title><link>http://localhost:1313/support/event-rental/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>http://localhost:1313/support/event-rental/</guid><description>&lt;p>Event rental information covers available spaces, capacity, rental policies, and booking details. Contact the museum to reserve a room for your next event.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Upstairs</title><link>http://localhost:1313/exhibitions/upstairs/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>http://localhost:1313/exhibitions/upstairs/</guid><description>&lt;p>The upstairs galleries feature rotating exhibitions and curated displays that highlight local history, art, and cultural programs. Explore this upper-level space for changing installations and interpretive exhibits.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Visitor Info</title><link>http://localhost:1313/visitor-info/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><g